  "upload": {
    "title": "How Does Samsung Keep Your Video Level? 📱 #shorts",
    "description": "He flips upside down, but the video doesn't. How? 📱\n\nThe Galaxy S26 FE's Super Steady with Horizontal Lock uses the phone's gyro sensor to track which way is down in real time. It records with the ultra-wide camera, crops the middle of that wide frame, and turns the crop the opposite way whenever the phone tilts, so the horizon stays level even through a full 360° spin. The trade-off: it records at a lower resolution than normal video, because it's using only part of the sensor.\n\nA gimbal in your pocket. 👇\n\nSubscribe to Top Techs for more mind-blowing tech in under a minute.",
